4
00:01:16,857 --> 00:01:20,588
- You cannot pass!
- Gandalf!

5
00:01:25,465 --> 00:01:30,801
I am a servant of the Secret
Fire, wielder of the flame of Anor.

6
00:01:38,745 --> 00:01:41,509
Go back to the Shadow.

7
00:01:42,415 --> 00:01:46,215
The dark fire will not avail you, flame of Udun!

8
00:01:50,088 --> 00:01:54,582
You shall not pass!

9
00:02:21,752 --> 00:02:23,413
No! No!

10
00:02:23,621 --> 00:02:25,589
Gandalf!

11
00:02:33,197 --> 00:02:34,926
Fly, you fools.

12
00:02:35,566 --> 00:02:37,431
No!

13
00:02:39,403 --> 00:02:41,462
Gandalf!

14
00:03:50,138 --> 00:03:51,969
Gandalf!

15
00:03:52,974 --> 00:03:55,203
What is it, Mr. Frodo?

16
00:03:57,144 --> 00:03:58,873
Nothing.

17
00:04:06,153 --> 00:04:08,212
Just a dream.

18
00:04:21,401 --> 00:04:22,595
Can you see the bottom?

19
00:04:23,870 --> 00:04:26,997
No! Don't look down, Sam! Just keep going!

20
00:04:37,850 --> 00:04:39,977
Catch it! Grab it, Mr. Frodo!

21
00:04:43,089 --> 00:04:45,057
Mr. Frodo!

22
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:49,389
I think I've found the bottom.

23
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:57,792
Bogs and rope, and goodness knows what.

24
00:04:57,969 --> 00:05:01,200
It's not natural. None of it.

25
00:05:04,309 --> 00:05:06,368
- What's in this?
- Nothing.

26
00:05:07,746 --> 00:05:08,804
Just a bit of seasoning.

27
00:05:09,414 --> 00:05:12,212
I thought maybe if we was having a
roast chicken one night or something.

28
00:05:12,751 --> 00:05:14,980
Roast chicken?!

29
00:05:15,586 --> 00:05:16,848
You never know.

30
00:05:17,321 --> 00:05:20,256
Sam. My dear Sam.

31
00:05:21,959 --> 00:05:25,895
It's very special, that. It's
the best salt in all the Shire.

32
00:05:27,164 --> 00:05:29,155
It is special.

33
00:05:33,036 --> 00:05:34,936
It's a little bit of home.

34
00:05:38,242 --> 00:05:40,676
We can't leave this here for someone to follow us down.

35
00:05:41,178 --> 00:05:44,636
Who's gonna follow us down here, Mr. Frodo?

36
00:05:45,482 --> 00:05:49,316
It's a shame, really. Lady Galadriel gave me that.

37
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:51,954
Real Elvish rope.

38
00:05:52,823 --> 00:05:55,257
Well, there's nothing for it. It's one of my knots.

39
00:05:55,425 --> 00:05:57,393
Won't come free in a hurry.

40
00:06:06,268 --> 00:06:08,395
Real Elvish rope.

41
00:06:22,551 --> 00:06:27,045
Mordor. The one place in Middle-earth
we don't want to see any closer.

42
00:06:27,222 --> 00:06:29,417
And it's the one place we're trying to get to.

43
00:06:30,158 --> 00:06:31,921
It's just where we can't get.

44
00:06:33,395 --> 00:06:36,330
Let's face it, Mr. Frodo, we're lost.

45
00:06:38,667 --> 00:06:41,431
I don't think Gandalf meant for us to come this way.

46
00:06:43,071 --> 00:06:46,370
He didn't mean for a lot of things to happen, Sam...

47
00:06:47,242 --> 00:06:48,709
...but they did.

48
00:07:01,822 --> 00:07:02,754
Mr. Frodo?

49
00:07:06,693 --> 00:07:08,092
It's the Ring, isn't it?

50
00:07:09,195 --> 00:07:11,663
It's getting heavier.

51
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:27,040
- What food have we got left?
- Let me see.

52
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,839
Oh, yes. Lovely.

53
00:07:30,016 --> 00:07:32,780
Lembas bread. And look!

54
00:07:35,221 --> 00:07:37,484
More lembas bread.

55
00:07:48,233 --> 00:07:50,201
I don't usually hold with foreign food...

56
00:07:50,402 --> 00:07:53,394
...but this Elvish stuff, it's not bad.

57
00:07:54,273 --> 00:07:57,731
Nothing ever dampens your spirits, does it, Sam?

58
00:08:03,548 --> 00:08:05,846
Those rain clouds might.

59
00:08:40,150 --> 00:08:42,914
This looks strangely familiar.

60
00:08:43,486 --> 00:08:46,011
It's because we've been here before.

61
00:08:46,189 --> 00:08:48,749
We're going in circles.

62
00:08:49,492 --> 00:08:51,357
What is that horrid stink?

63
00:08:51,528 --> 00:08:53,723
I warrant there's a nasty bog nearby.

64
00:08:53,897 --> 00:08:55,831
- Can you smell it?
- Yes.

65
00:08:57,867 --> 00:09:00,097
I can smell it.

66
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:05,774
We're not alone.

67
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:23,516
The thieves. The thieves.

68
00:09:23,691 --> 00:09:27,650
The filthy little thieves.

69
00:09:28,329 --> 00:09:30,490
Where is it?

70
00:09:30,665 --> 00:09:33,361
Where is it?

71
00:09:34,068 --> 00:09:37,265
They stole it from us.

72
00:09:37,472 --> 00:09:41,670
My precious.

73
00:09:42,543 --> 00:09:45,808
Curse them, we hates them!

74
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:50,076
It's ours, it is, and we wants it!

75
00:10:45,171 --> 00:10:46,967
This is Sting.

76
00:10:47,138 --> 00:10:48,662
You've seen it before...

77
00:10:48,873 --> 00:10:51,341
haven't you, Gollum?

78
00:10:55,413 --> 00:10:58,905
Release him or I'll cut your throat.

79
00:11:14,933 --> 00:11:16,695
It burns!

80
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:19,198
It burns us!

81
00:11:20,671 --> 00:11:22,138
It freezes!

82
00:11:23,941 --> 00:11:26,205
Nasty Elves twisted it.

83
00:11:26,376 --> 00:11:29,038
- Take it off us!
- Quiet, you!

84
00:11:32,449 --> 00:11:36,714
It's hopeless. Every Orc in
Mordor's going to hear this racket.

85
00:11:36,886 --> 00:11:39,480
- Let's just tie him up and leave him.
- No!

86
00:11:39,755 --> 00:11:43,247
That would kill us! Kill us!

87
00:11:43,426 --> 00:11:46,122
It's no more than you deserve!

88
00:11:47,830 --> 00:11:49,855
Maybe he does deserve to die.

89
00:11:52,268 --> 00:11:55,704
But now that I see him, I do pity him.

90
00:11:59,175 --> 00:12:04,010
We be nice to them if they be nice to us.

91
00:12:04,247 --> 00:12:07,011
Take it off us.

92
00:12:10,119 --> 00:12:14,055
We swears to do what you wants.

93
00:12:14,223 --> 00:12:16,157
We swears.

94
00:12:16,459 --> 00:12:18,893
There's no promise you can make that I can trust.

95
00:12:21,595 --> 00:12:23,324
We swears...

96
00:12:23,597 --> 00:12:28,330
to serve the master of the precious.

97
00:12:29,970 --> 00:12:32,302
We will swear on...

98
00:12:32,473 --> 00:12:34,441
on the precious.

99
00:12:34,608 --> 00:12:36,803
Gollum. Gollum.

100
00:12:36,977 --> 00:12:41,107
The Ring is treacherous. It will hold you to your word.

101
00:12:41,949 --> 00:12:43,280
Yes...

102
00:12:43,851 --> 00:12:46,342
on the precious.

103
00:12:48,722 --> 00:12:51,156
On the precious.

104
00:12:52,326 --> 00:12:53,816
I don't believe you!

105
00:12:55,863 --> 00:12:59,321
- Get down! I said, down!
- Sam!

106
00:12:59,567 --> 00:13:01,262
He's trying to trick us.

107
00:13:01,435 --> 00:13:04,427
If we let him go, he'll throttle us in our sleep.

108
00:13:15,848 --> 00:13:20,376
- You know the way to Mordor?
- Yes.

109
00:13:23,322 --> 00:13:25,051
You've been there before?

110
00:13:26,058 --> 00:13:27,650
Yes.

111
00:13:38,570 --> 00:13:41,198
You will lead us to the Black Gate.

112
00:13:49,781 --> 00:13:53,649
To the Gate, to the Gate! To
the Gate, the master says. Yes!

113
00:13:53,819 --> 00:13:58,619
No! We won't go back. Not there. Not to him.

114
00:13:58,789 --> 00:14:03,021
They can't make us. Gollum! Gollum!

115
00:14:03,227 --> 00:14:06,663
But we swore to serve the master of the precious.

116
00:14:06,864 --> 00:14:12,825
No. Ashes and dust and thirst
there is, and pits, pits, pits.

117
00:14:13,004 --> 00:14:15,871
And Orcses, thousands of Orcses.

118
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:21,171
And always the Great Eye watching, watching.

119
00:14:24,148 --> 00:14:27,947
Hey! Come back now! Come back!

120
00:14:30,353 --> 00:14:32,583
There! What did I tell you?

121
00:14:32,756 --> 00:14:34,986
He's run off, the old villain.

122
00:14:35,191 --> 00:14:37,682
So much for his promises.

123
00:14:37,894 --> 00:14:39,452
This way, Hobbits.

124
00:14:39,729 --> 00:14:41,754
Follow me!

125
00:14:55,611 --> 00:14:57,010
Merry!

126
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,470
Merry!

127
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:08,753
You're late. Our master grows impatient.

128
00:15:08,957 --> 00:15:10,754
He wants the Shire-rats now.

129
00:15:11,627 --> 00:15:16,223
I don't take orders from Orc-maggots.

130
00:15:17,266 --> 00:15:20,326
Saruman will have his prize.

131
00:15:20,502 --> 00:15:23,699
We will deliver them.

132
00:15:29,911 --> 00:15:31,276
Merry!

133
00:15:32,012 --> 00:15:33,775
Merry? Wake up.

134
00:15:37,250 --> 00:15:39,115
My friend is sick.

135
00:15:39,553 --> 00:15:42,215
He needs water. Please!

136
00:15:42,989 --> 00:15:46,925
Sick, is he? Give him some medicine, boys!

137
00:15:50,163 --> 00:15:51,824
Stop it!

138
00:15:54,034 --> 00:15:56,662
Can't take his draught!

139
00:15:59,339 --> 00:16:01,899
- Leave him alone!
- Why?

140
00:16:02,442 --> 00:16:04,808
You want some?

141
00:16:05,545 --> 00:16:08,912
Then keep your mouth shut.

142
00:16:12,319 --> 00:16:14,344
Merry.

143
00:16:15,255 --> 00:16:16,745
Hello, Pip.

144
00:16:18,592 --> 00:16:21,025
- You're hurt.
- I'm fine.

145
00:16:21,193 --> 00:16:23,684
- It was just an act.
- An act?

146
00:16:24,363 --> 00:16:27,230
See? I fooled you too.

147
00:16:29,935 --> 00:16:31,664
Don't worry about me, Pippin.

148
00:16:33,972 --> 00:16:35,963
What is it? What do you smell?

149
00:16:36,941 --> 00:16:38,238
Man-flesh.

150
00:16:40,378 --> 00:16:42,744
They've picked up our trail.

151
00:16:43,848 --> 00:16:44,974
Aragorn.

152
00:16:46,684 --> 00:16:48,515
Let's move!

153
00:17:12,075 --> 00:17:14,600
Their pace has quickened.

154
00:17:15,612 --> 00:17:17,580
They must have caught our scent.

155
00:17:17,748 --> 00:17:19,511
Hurry!

156
00:17:23,187 --> 00:17:24,916
Come on, Gimli!

157
00:17:28,759 --> 00:17:31,057
Three days and nights pursuit.

158
00:17:31,228 --> 00:17:34,197
No food. No rest.

159
00:17:34,364 --> 00:17:38,356
And no sign of our quarry, but what bare rock can tell.

160
00:18:09,764 --> 00:18:12,961
Not idly do the leaves of Lorien fall.

161
00:18:14,302 --> 00:18:16,668
They may yet be alive.

162
00:18:17,506 --> 00:18:20,134
Less than a day ahead of us. Come.

163
00:18:22,744 --> 00:18:25,235
Come, Gimli! We're gaining on them!

164
00:18:25,413 --> 00:18:29,713
I'm wasted on cross-country. We
Dwarves are natural sprinters.

165
00:18:30,252 --> 00:18:33,517
Very dangerous over short distances.

166
00:18:45,265 --> 00:18:46,994
Rohan.

167
00:18:47,166 --> 00:18:49,964
Home of the Horse-lords.

168
00:18:51,170 --> 00:18:53,730
There's something strange at work here.

169
00:18:53,907 --> 00:18:56,876
Some evil gives speed to these creatures.

170
00:18:57,043 --> 00:19:00,012
Sets its will against us.

171
00:19:05,218 --> 00:19:08,085
Legolas! What do your Elf-eyes see?

172
00:19:08,254 --> 00:19:10,814
The Uruks turn northeast.

173
00:19:11,658 --> 00:19:13,819
They are taking the Hobbits to Isengard.

174
00:19:14,694 --> 00:19:15,956
Saruman.

175
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:27,567
The world is changing.

176
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:33,336
Who now has the strength to stand
against the armies of Isengard...

177
00:19:34,046 --> 00:19:36,776
and Mordor?

178
00:19:38,483 --> 00:19:44,114
To stand against the might of Sauron and Saruman...

179
00:19:44,288 --> 00:19:47,917
and the union of the two towers?

180
00:19:54,432 --> 00:19:57,401
Together, my Lord Sauron...

181
00:19:57,568 --> 00:20:01,095
we shall rule this Middle-earth.

182
00:20:17,187 --> 00:20:21,453
The Old World will burn in the fires of industry.

183
00:20:22,025 --> 00:20:25,290
The forests will fall.

184
00:20:27,197 --> 00:20:30,064
A new order will rise.

185
00:20:31,134 --> 00:20:36,037
We will drive the machine of war
with the sword and the spear...

186
00:20:36,206 --> 00:20:40,165
and the iron fists of the Orc.

187
00:20:52,688 --> 00:20:55,919
I want them armed and ready to march within two weeks!

188
00:20:56,091 --> 00:20:57,718
But, my lord, there are too many!

189
00:20:57,893 --> 00:21:00,919
They cannot all be armed in
time, we don't have the means.

190
00:21:01,096 --> 00:21:04,155
Build a dam, block the stream,
work the furnaces night and day.

191
00:21:04,799 --> 00:21:07,165
We don't have enough fuel to feed the fires.

192
00:21:08,536 --> 00:21:12,802
The Forest of Fangorn lies on our doorstep.

193
00:21:14,242 --> 00:21:16,574
- Burn it.
- Yes.

194
00:21:17,311 --> 00:21:19,609
We will fight for you.

195
00:21:19,781 --> 00:21:21,749
Swear it.

196
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:37,027
We will die for Saruman.

197
00:21:38,132 --> 00:21:40,123
The Horse-Men took your lands.

198
00:21:40,301 --> 00:21:44,829
They drove your people into the
hills to scratch a living off rocks.

199
00:21:45,006 --> 00:21:46,439
Murderers!

200
00:21:47,375 --> 00:21:49,467
Take back the lands they stole from you.

201
00:21:49,676 --> 00:21:51,438
Burn every village!

202
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:59,811
We have only to remove those who oppose us.

203
00:22:00,286 --> 00:22:02,811
It will begin in Rohan.

204
00:22:03,556 --> 00:22:07,083
Too long have these peasants stood against you.

205
00:22:07,259 --> 00:22:09,056
But no more.

206
00:22:09,228 --> 00:22:11,492
Eothain! Eothain!

207
00:22:13,666 --> 00:22:16,328
You take your sister. You'll go faster with just two.

208
00:22:16,702 --> 00:22:19,364
Papa says Eothain must not ride Garulf.

209
00:22:19,538 --> 00:22:21,199
He is too big for him.

210
00:22:21,407 --> 00:22:24,376
Listen to me. You must ride
to Edoras and raise the alarm.

211
00:22:24,577 --> 00:22:27,068
- Do you understand me?
- Yes, Mama.

212
00:22:27,379 --> 00:22:30,280
I don't want to leave. I don't want to go, Mama.

213
00:22:30,449 --> 00:22:34,180
Freda, I will find you there.

214
00:22:39,090 --> 00:22:40,785
Quickly!

215
00:22:47,198 --> 00:22:48,756
Go, child.

216
00:23:01,645 --> 00:23:03,545
Rohan, my lord...

217
00:23:04,014 --> 00:23:06,744
is ready to fall.

218
00:23:17,995 --> 00:23:19,519
Theodred.

219
00:23:19,730 --> 00:23:21,357
Find the king's son!

220
00:23:37,814 --> 00:23:43,844
- Mordor will pay for this.
- These Orcs are not from Mordor.

221
00:23:44,754 --> 00:23:47,587
My Lord Eomer, over here!

222
00:23:56,398 --> 00:23:58,195
He's alive.

223
00:24:28,996 --> 00:24:31,089
Theodred.

224
00:24:44,478 --> 00:24:47,504
Your son is badly wounded, my lord.

225
00:24:47,915 --> 00:24:50,406
He was ambushed by Orcs.

226
00:24:51,952 --> 00:24:55,581
If we don't defend our country,
Saruman will take it by force.

227
00:24:55,956 --> 00:24:58,446
That is a lie.

228
00:25:00,660 --> 00:25:05,460
Saruman the White has ever been our friend and ally.

229
00:25:07,132 --> 00:25:09,123
Grima.

230
00:25:10,569 --> 00:25:12,503
Grima.

231
00:25:15,040 --> 00:25:16,530
Grima.

232
00:25:17,342 --> 00:25:20,402
Orcs are roaming freely across our lands.

233
00:25:20,812 --> 00:25:24,407
Unchecked. Unchallenged. Killing at will.

234
00:25:25,083 --> 00:25:27,984
Orcs bearing the White Hand of Saruman.

235
00:25:35,827 --> 00:25:41,595
Why do you lay these troubles
on an already troubled mind?

236
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:44,268
Can you not see?

237
00:25:44,436 --> 00:25:49,463
Your uncle is wearied by your malcontent...

238
00:25:49,674 --> 00:25:52,199
your warmongering.

239
00:25:54,412 --> 00:25:56,380
Warmongering?

240
00:25:56,547 --> 00:25:58,708
How long is it since Saruman bought you?

241
00:25:59,550 --> 00:26:01,915
What was the promised price, Grima?

242
00:26:02,152 --> 00:26:05,747
When all the Men are dead, you will
take your share of the treasure?

243
00:26:18,234 --> 00:26:20,862
Too long have you watched my sister.

244
00:26:21,071 --> 00:26:23,039
Too long have you haunted her steps.

245
00:26:31,114 --> 00:26:35,448
You see much, Eomer, son of Eomund.

246
00:26:35,618 --> 00:26:36,777
Too much.

247
00:26:39,121 --> 00:26:43,922
You are banished forthwith from the kingdom of Rohan...

248
00:26:44,093 --> 00:26:48,894
and all its domains under pain of death.

249
00:26:49,365 --> 00:26:51,697
You have no authority here.

250
00:26:51,867 --> 00:26:54,335
Your orders mean nothing.

251
00:26:54,870 --> 00:26:58,704
This order does not come from me.

252
00:26:58,874 --> 00:27:01,035
It comes from the king.

253
00:27:01,643 --> 00:27:04,236
He signed it this morning.

254
00:27:35,809 --> 00:27:38,505
Keep breathing. That's the key.

255
00:27:38,745 --> 00:27:40,440
Breathe.

256
00:27:44,551 --> 00:27:48,385
They've run as if the very whips
of their masters were behind them.

257
00:28:04,538 --> 00:28:06,563
We're not going no further...

258
00:28:06,740 --> 00:28:08,730
until we've had a breather.

259
00:28:09,275 --> 00:28:11,242
Get a fire going!

260
00:28:15,313 --> 00:28:16,871
Merry!

261
00:28:17,248 --> 00:28:18,579
Merry!

262
00:28:20,285 --> 00:28:25,484
I think we might have made a
mistake leaving the Shire, Pippin.

263
00:28:34,966 --> 00:28:37,161
What's making that noise?

264
00:28:38,736 --> 00:28:40,203
It's the trees.

265
00:28:40,939 --> 00:28:41,997
What?

266
00:28:42,340 --> 00:28:46,174
You remember the Old Forest,
on the borders of Buckland?

267
00:28:46,344 --> 00:28:50,838
Folk used to say there was something in
the water that made the trees grow tall...

268
00:28:51,015 --> 00:28:52,539
and come alive.

269
00:28:52,784 --> 00:28:54,479
Alive?

270
00:28:55,353 --> 00:28:57,048
Trees that could whisper...

271
00:28:58,056 --> 00:29:00,523
talk to each other...

272
00:29:00,691 --> 00:29:02,488
even move.

273
00:29:04,128 --> 00:29:06,358
I'm starving.

274
00:29:06,530 --> 00:29:10,590
We ain't had nothing but maggoty
bread for three stinking days.

275
00:29:10,967 --> 00:29:12,229
Yeah!

276
00:29:12,435 --> 00:29:15,700
Why can't we have some meat?!

277
00:29:18,074 --> 00:29:20,269
What about them?

278
00:29:20,443 --> 00:29:22,343
They're fresh.

279
00:29:23,012 --> 00:29:26,778
They are not for eating.

280
00:29:32,755 --> 00:29:34,723
What about their legs?

281
00:29:34,924 --> 00:29:37,222
They don't need those.

282
00:29:38,694 --> 00:29:41,891
- They look tasty.
- Get back, scum!

283
00:29:43,699 --> 00:29:48,601
The prisoners go to Saruman. Alive and unspoiled.

284
00:29:48,970 --> 00:29:50,904
Alive?

285
00:29:53,875 --> 00:29:58,141
Why alive? Do they give good sport?

286
00:30:00,549 --> 00:30:03,916
They have something. An Elvish weapon.

287
00:30:04,085 --> 00:30:07,111
The master wants it for the war.

288
00:30:10,025 --> 00:30:11,890
They think we have the Ring.

289
00:30:12,060 --> 00:30:14,493
As soon as they find out we don't, we're dead.

290
00:30:16,363 --> 00:30:18,331
Just a mouthful...

291
00:30:18,499 --> 00:30:19,693
a bit of the flank.

292
00:30:26,507 --> 00:30:30,068
Looks like meat's back on the menu, boys.

293
00:30:36,683 --> 00:30:37,945
Pippin.

294
00:30:38,117 --> 00:30:39,812
Let's go.

295
00:30:48,261 --> 00:30:49,751
Go on.

296
00:30:49,963 --> 00:30:51,430
Call for help.

297
00:30:52,832 --> 00:30:53,924
Squeal.

298
00:30:54,133 --> 00:30:57,296
No one's going to save you now.

299
00:31:06,479 --> 00:31:07,878
Pippin!

300
00:31:32,169 --> 00:31:34,660
A red sun rises.

301
00:31:35,172 --> 00:31:38,107
Blood has been spilled this night.

302
00:32:09,272 --> 00:32:11,137
Riders of Rohan...

303
00:32:11,574 --> 00:32:14,008
what news from the Mark?

304
00:32:41,770 --> 00:32:46,173
What business does an Elf, a Man
and a Dwarf have in the Riddermark?

305
00:32:46,975 --> 00:32:48,237
Speak quickly!

306
00:32:48,577 --> 00:32:53,241
Give me your name, horse-master,
and I shall give you mine.

307
00:33:02,390 --> 00:33:04,915
I would cut off your head, Dwarf...

308
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:07,726
if it stood but a little higher from the ground.

309
00:33:08,763 --> 00:33:10,822
You would die before your stroke fell.

310
00:33:19,540 --> 00:33:21,440
I am Aragorn, son of Arathorn.

311
00:33:21,776 --> 00:33:25,973
This is Gimli, son of Gloin, and
Legolas of the Woodland Realm.

312
00:33:26,146 --> 00:33:29,377
We are friends of Rohan and of Theoden, your king.

313
00:33:31,118 --> 00:33:34,884
Theoden no longer recognizes friend from foe.

314
00:33:35,122 --> 00:33:37,317
Not even his own kin.

315
00:33:41,828 --> 00:33:43,795
Saruman has poisoned the mind of the king...

316
00:33:43,963 --> 00:33:45,897
and claimed lordship over these lands.

317
00:33:47,867 --> 00:33:50,859
My company are those loyal to Rohan.

318
00:33:51,036 --> 00:33:52,799
And for that, we are banished.

319
00:33:54,874 --> 00:33:58,173
The White Wizard is cunning.

320
00:33:58,844 --> 00:34:01,244
He walks here and there, they say...

321
00:34:01,447 --> 00:34:03,381
as an old man hooded and cloaked.

322
00:34:05,317 --> 00:34:09,083
And everywhere, his spies slip past our nets.

323
00:34:09,255 --> 00:34:11,485
We are no spies.

324
00:34:11,657 --> 00:34:14,592
We track a party of Uruk-hai
westward across the plain.

325
00:34:14,894 --> 00:34:17,226
They have taken two of our friends captive.

326
00:34:18,030 --> 00:34:20,498
The Uruks are destroyed. We
slaughtered them during the night.

327
00:34:20,666 --> 00:34:23,829
But there were two Hobbits. Did
you see two Hobbits with them?

328
00:34:24,003 --> 00:34:26,971
They would be small. Only children to your eyes.

329
00:34:30,308 --> 00:34:32,298
We left none alive.

330
00:34:32,943 --> 00:34:35,912
We piled the carcasses and burned them.

331
00:34:41,385 --> 00:34:42,613
Dead?

332
00:34:45,622 --> 00:34:47,317
I am sorry.

333
00:34:52,896 --> 00:34:55,194
Hasufel! Arod!

334
00:34:57,000 --> 00:35:01,664
May these horses bear you to better
fortune than their former masters.

335
00:35:02,873 --> 00:35:04,465
Farewell.

336
00:35:09,680 --> 00:35:11,910
Look for your friends.

337
00:35:12,382 --> 00:35:14,612
But do not trust to hope.

338
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:18,879
It has forsaken these lands.

339
00:35:19,088 --> 00:35:21,079
We ride north!

340
00:36:11,672 --> 00:36:13,503
It's one of their wee belts.

341
00:36:14,955 --> 00:36:18,955
[Sindarin] <i>Hiro hyn hîdh ab ’wanath.</i>
[English] May they find peace after death.

342
00:36:27,321 --> 00:36:29,346
We failed them.

343
00:36:43,403 --> 00:36:45,564
A Hobbit lay here.

344
00:36:47,473 --> 00:36:49,100
And the other.

345
00:36:59,918 --> 00:37:01,510
They crawled.

346
00:37:05,624 --> 00:37:07,717
Their hands were bound.

347
00:37:19,871 --> 00:37:21,702
Their bonds were cut.

348
00:37:37,188 --> 00:37:39,315
They ran over here.

349
00:37:42,959 --> 00:37:44,153
They were followed.

350
00:37:47,364 --> 00:37:49,093
The belt!

351
00:37:53,003 --> 00:37:54,129
Run!

352
00:37:57,874 --> 00:37:59,205
Tracks lead away from the battle...

353
00:38:04,014 --> 00:38:06,107
into Fangorn Forest.

354
00:38:07,017 --> 00:38:08,450
Fangorn?

355
00:38:08,618 --> 00:38:11,246
What madness drove them in there?

356
00:38:29,004 --> 00:38:31,996
Did we lose him? I think we lost him.

357
00:38:38,713 --> 00:38:42,149
I'm going to rip out your filthy little innards!

358
00:38:48,389 --> 00:38:49,378
Come here!

359
00:38:54,896 --> 00:38:57,456
Trees. Climb a tree.

360
00:39:06,774 --> 00:39:08,503
He's gone.

361
00:39:20,587 --> 00:39:22,919
Merry!

362
00:39:34,401 --> 00:39:38,804
Let's put a maggot hole in your belly!

363
00:39:45,911 --> 00:39:47,469
Run, Merry!

364
00:39:57,256 --> 00:40:01,590
Little Orcs.

365
00:40:01,761 --> 00:40:04,092
It's talking, Merry. The tree is talking.

366
00:40:04,262 --> 00:40:06,162
Tree?

367
00:40:06,331 --> 00:40:09,323
I am no tree!

368
00:40:09,567 --> 00:40:11,728
I am an Ent.

369
00:40:12,303 --> 00:40:14,430
A tree-herder.

370
00:40:15,006 --> 00:40:16,974
A shepherd of the forest.

371
00:40:17,142 --> 00:40:18,507
Don't talk to it, Merry.

372
00:40:19,010 --> 00:40:20,477
Don't encourage it!

373
00:40:20,678 --> 00:40:24,910
Treebeard, some call me.

374
00:40:25,083 --> 00:40:27,051
And whose side are you on?

375
00:40:27,652 --> 00:40:29,279
Side?

376
00:40:29,487 --> 00:40:32,354
I am on nobody's side...

377
00:40:32,724 --> 00:40:38,060
because nobody's on my side, little Orc.

378
00:40:38,863 --> 00:40:43,493
Nobody cares for the woods anymore.

379
00:40:43,902 --> 00:40:46,301
We're not Orcs! We're Hobbits!

380
00:40:46,470 --> 00:40:48,768
Hobbits?

381
00:40:50,007 --> 00:40:54,875
Never heard of a Hobbit before.

382
00:40:56,078 --> 00:41:00,572
Sounds like Orc mischief to me!

383
00:41:00,750 --> 00:41:02,877
They come with fire.

384
00:41:03,085 --> 00:41:05,645
They come with axes.

385
00:41:05,855 --> 00:41:10,656
Gnawing, biting, breaking, hacking, burning!

386
00:41:10,860 --> 00:41:14,660
- Destroyers and usurpers! Curse them!
- No!

387
00:41:14,897 --> 00:41:17,730
You don't understand. We're Hobbits!

388
00:41:17,934 --> 00:41:19,731
Halflings!

389
00:41:19,902 --> 00:41:20,994
Shire-folk!

390
00:41:21,204 --> 00:41:23,536
Maybe you are...

391
00:41:23,840 --> 00:41:27,469
and maybe you aren't.

392
00:41:28,578 --> 00:41:32,480
The White Wizard will know.

393
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:35,216
The White Wizard?

394
00:41:36,752 --> 00:41:38,241
Saruman.

395
00:41:50,831 --> 00:41:52,492
See? See?

396
00:41:52,733 --> 00:41:55,133
We've led you out.

397
00:41:55,302 --> 00:41:57,793
Hurry, Hobbitses. Hurry!

398
00:42:00,908 --> 00:42:03,376
Very lucky we find you.

399
00:42:10,050 --> 00:42:11,779
Nice Hobbit.

400
00:42:14,688 --> 00:42:17,953
It's a bog. He's led us into a swamp.

401
00:42:18,125 --> 00:42:20,753
A swamp, yes, yes.

402
00:42:21,528 --> 00:42:26,226
Come, master. We will take you
on safe paths through the mist.

403
00:42:28,568 --> 00:42:32,004
Come, Hobbits! Come! We go quickly.

404
00:42:35,275 --> 00:42:37,903
I found it. I did.

405
00:42:38,111 --> 00:42:40,773
The way through the marshes.

406
00:42:40,980 --> 00:42:44,472
Orcs don't use it. Orcs don't know it.

407
00:42:44,684 --> 00:42:48,745
They go around for miles and miles.

408
00:42:48,955 --> 00:42:50,388
Come quickly.

409
00:42:50,590 --> 00:42:54,650
Soft and quick as shadows we must be.

410
00:42:55,827 --> 00:42:59,160
I hate this place. It's too quiet.

411
00:42:59,331 --> 00:43:01,595
There's been no sight nor sound of a bird for two days.

412
00:43:01,767 --> 00:43:05,134
No, no birdses to eat.

413
00:43:05,370 --> 00:43:09,602
No crunchable birdses.

414
00:43:10,208 --> 00:43:13,074
We are famished! Yes!

415
00:43:13,244 --> 00:43:17,544
Famished we are, precious!

416
00:43:32,496 --> 00:43:34,020
Here.

417
00:43:35,232 --> 00:43:37,223
What does it eats?

418
00:43:37,435 --> 00:43:39,403
Is it tasty?

419
00:43:44,709 --> 00:43:47,303
It tries to chokes us!

420
00:43:47,578 --> 00:43:51,241
We can't eats Hobbit food!

421
00:43:52,950 --> 00:43:56,976
We must starve!

422
00:43:57,153 --> 00:43:59,519
Well, starve, then. And good riddance!

423
00:44:00,290 --> 00:44:02,484
Oh, cruel Hobbit.

424
00:44:02,691 --> 00:44:05,524
It does not care if we be hungry.

425
00:44:05,761 --> 00:44:10,494
Does not care if we should die.

426
00:44:11,133 --> 00:44:13,966
Not like master.

427
00:44:15,337 --> 00:44:17,430
Master cares.

428
00:44:18,607 --> 00:44:20,472
Master knows.

429
00:44:22,945 --> 00:44:24,913
Yes.

430
00:44:25,080 --> 00:44:27,708
Precious.

431
00:44:31,286 --> 00:44:34,915
Once it takes hold of us...

432
00:44:36,792 --> 00:44:40,956
it never lets go.

433
00:44:41,663 --> 00:44:42,823
Don't touch me!

434
00:45:15,295 --> 00:45:17,160
There are dead things!

435
00:45:17,330 --> 00:45:19,093
Dead faces in the water.

436
00:45:23,937 --> 00:45:27,896
All dead. All rotten.

437
00:45:28,408 --> 00:45:32,174
Elves and Men and Orcses.

438
00:45:32,379 --> 00:45:36,007
A great battle long ago.

439
00:45:36,816 --> 00:45:38,545
Dead Marshes.

440
00:45:38,751 --> 00:45:41,481
Yes. Yes, that is their name.

441
00:45:43,189 --> 00:45:44,918
This way.

442
00:45:45,124 --> 00:45:47,888
Don't follow the lights.

443
00:45:49,628 --> 00:45:53,496
Careful now! Or Hobbits go
down to join the dead ones...

444
00:45:53,699 --> 00:45:57,795
and light little candles of their own.

445
00:46:23,994 --> 00:46:25,461
Frodo!

446
00:47:09,939 --> 00:47:14,602
- Gollum?
- Don't follow the lights.

447
00:47:14,776 --> 00:47:16,641
- Gollum!
- Mr. Frodo!

448
00:47:16,811 --> 00:47:18,676
Are you all right?

449
00:47:47,576 --> 00:47:50,545
So bright.

450
00:47:50,745 --> 00:47:54,545
So beautiful.

451
00:47:54,716 --> 00:47:58,583
Our precious.

452
00:48:00,054 --> 00:48:01,544
What did you say?

453
00:48:01,755 --> 00:48:03,916
Master should be resting.

454
00:48:04,091 --> 00:48:08,151
Master needs to keep up his strength.

455
00:48:10,129 --> 00:48:13,394
- Who are you?
- Mustn't ask us. Not its business.

456
00:48:13,566 --> 00:48:15,056
Gollum. Gollum.

457
00:48:15,235 --> 00:48:17,032
Gandalf told me you were one of the river-folk.

458
00:48:17,203 --> 00:48:21,299
Cold be heart and hand and bone
Cold be travelers far from home

459
00:48:21,474 --> 00:48:23,032
He said your life was a sad story.

460
00:48:23,243 --> 00:48:27,771
They do not see what lies ahead
When sun has failed and moon is dead

461
00:48:27,947 --> 00:48:30,939
You were not so very different from a Hobbit once.

462
00:48:31,150 --> 00:48:32,879
Were you?

463
00:48:35,121 --> 00:48:37,351
Smeagol.

464
00:48:42,061 --> 00:48:44,586
What did you call me?

465
00:48:45,931 --> 00:48:48,695
That was your name once, wasn't it?

466
00:48:49,268 --> 00:48:51,634
A long time ago.

467
00:48:52,471 --> 00:48:54,632
My name.

468
00:48:55,707 --> 00:48:57,197
My name.

469
00:49:04,082 --> 00:49:06,550
Smeagol.

470
00:49:10,688 --> 00:49:12,315
Black Riders!

471
00:49:12,490 --> 00:49:13,821
Hide! Hide!

472
00:49:24,402 --> 00:49:26,700
Come on, Frodo. Come on!

473
00:49:26,871 --> 00:49:30,500
Quick! They will see us! They will see us!

474
00:49:31,275 --> 00:49:33,936
- I thought they were dead.
- Dead?

475
00:49:34,110 --> 00:49:37,079
No, you cannot kill them. No.

476
00:50:04,240 --> 00:50:05,332
Wraiths!

477
00:50:05,542 --> 00:50:07,737
Wraiths on wings!

478
00:50:15,751 --> 00:50:17,776
They are calling for it.

479
00:50:18,020 --> 00:50:21,546
They are calling for the precious.

480
00:50:23,691 --> 00:50:25,818
Mr. Frodo! It's all right.

481
00:50:25,993 --> 00:50:27,255
I'm here.

482
00:50:43,277 --> 00:50:44,801
Hurry, Hobbits.

483
00:50:45,380 --> 00:50:49,316
The Black Gate is very close.

484
00:50:56,190 --> 00:50:58,055
Orc blood.

485
00:51:08,001 --> 00:51:09,764
These are strange tracks.

486
00:51:11,037 --> 00:51:13,062
The air is so close in here.

487
00:51:14,207 --> 00:51:16,640
This forest is old.

488
00:51:17,443 --> 00:51:19,434
Very old.

489
00:51:21,213 --> 00:51:23,511
Full of memory...

490
00:51:26,118 --> 00:51:28,450
and anger.

491
00:51:34,627 --> 00:51:37,528
The trees are speaking to each other.

492
00:51:37,696 --> 00:51:39,186
Gimli!

493
00:51:39,365 --> 00:51:41,299
Lower your ax.

494
00:51:44,103 --> 00:51:46,867
They have feelings, my friend.

495
00:51:47,406 --> 00:51:49,397
The Elves began it.

496
00:51:49,608 --> 00:51:54,341
Waking up the trees, teaching them to speak.

497
00:51:54,847 --> 00:51:57,212
Talking trees.

498
00:51:57,849 --> 00:52:00,875
What do trees have to talk about?

499
00:52:01,052 --> 00:52:04,215
Except the consistency of squirrel droppings.

500
00:52:07,235 --> 00:52:09,185
[Sindarin] <i>Aragorn, nad no ennas!</i>
[English] A thing to be there!

501
00:52:15,970 --> 00:52:17,794
[Sindarin] <i>Man cenich?</i>
[English] What do you see?

502
00:52:18,169 --> 00:52:20,602
The White Wizard approaches.

503
00:52:26,810 --> 00:52:31,110
Do not let him speak. He will put a spell on us.

504
00:52:40,691 --> 00:52:42,954
We must be quick.

505
00:52:58,541 --> 00:53:02,170
You are tracking the footsteps of two young Hobbits.

506
00:53:02,745 --> 00:53:04,144
Where are they?

507
00:53:04,313 --> 00:53:07,874
They passed this way the day before yesterday.

508
00:53:08,050 --> 00:53:12,316
They met someone they did not expect.

509
00:53:12,488 --> 00:53:14,615
Does that comfort you?

510
00:53:14,790 --> 00:53:16,758
Who are you?

511
00:53:18,227 --> 00:53:20,195
Show yourself!

512
00:53:29,104 --> 00:53:31,094
It cannot be.

513
00:53:34,074 --> 00:53:35,041
Forgive me.

514
00:53:36,710 --> 00:53:38,644
I mistook you for Saruman.

515
00:53:39,413 --> 00:53:42,177
I am Saruman.

516
00:53:43,717 --> 00:53:47,585
Or rather, Saruman as he should have been.

517
00:53:48,556 --> 00:53:50,046
You fell.

518
00:53:51,525 --> 00:53:54,050
Through fire...

519
00:53:54,228 --> 00:53:55,525
and water.

520
00:53:56,997 --> 00:53:59,522
From the lowest dungeon to the highest peak...

521
00:53:59,700 --> 00:54:03,397
I fought with the Balrog of Morgoth.

522
00:54:19,252 --> 00:54:21,982
Until at last I threw down my enemy...

523
00:54:22,155 --> 00:54:26,614
and smote his ruin upon the mountainside.

524
00:54:32,631 --> 00:54:35,191
Darkness took me...

525
00:54:35,968 --> 00:54:40,029
and I strayed out of thought and time.

526
00:54:40,806 --> 00:54:43,866
Stars wheeled overhead...

527
00:54:44,142 --> 00:54:48,636
and every day was as long as a life age of the Earth.

528
00:54:50,782 --> 00:54:52,909
But it was not the end.

529
00:54:53,151 --> 00:54:55,984
I felt life in me again.

530
00:54:57,923 --> 00:55:00,448
I've been sent back...

531
00:55:00,626 --> 00:55:02,184
until my task is done.

532
00:55:02,561 --> 00:55:04,461
Gandalf.

533
00:55:05,129 --> 00:55:07,120
Gandalf?

534
00:55:07,531 --> 00:55:09,328
Yes.

535
00:55:12,136 --> 00:55:13,933
That was what they used to call me.

536
00:55:16,807 --> 00:55:19,071
Gandalf the Grey.

537
00:55:20,411 --> 00:55:22,174
That was my name.

538
00:55:22,346 --> 00:55:23,779
Gandalf.

539
00:55:25,750 --> 00:55:27,809
I am Gandalf the White.

540
00:55:30,854 --> 00:55:33,914
And I come back to you now...

541
00:55:34,090 --> 00:55:36,581
at the turn of the tide.

542
00:55:37,694 --> 00:55:40,663
One stage of your journey is over. Another begins.

543
00:55:41,431 --> 00:55:44,594
- We must travel to Edoras with all speed.
- Edoras?

544
00:55:45,535 --> 00:55:47,560
That is no short distance!

545
00:55:47,837 --> 00:55:51,068
We hear of trouble in Rohan. It goes ill with the king.

546
00:55:51,241 --> 00:55:53,333
Yes, and it will not be easily cured.

547
00:55:53,509 --> 00:55:56,945
Then we have run all this way for nothing?

548
00:55:57,112 --> 00:55:59,103
Are we to leave those poor Hobbits here...

549
00:55:59,281 --> 00:56:03,445
in this horrid, dark, dank tree-infested...?

550
00:56:06,055 --> 00:56:09,218
I mean, charming...

551
00:56:09,391 --> 00:56:12,121
quite charming forest.

552
00:56:12,661 --> 00:56:16,324
It was more than mere chance that
brought Merry and Pippin to Fangorn.

553
00:56:16,532 --> 00:56:20,901
A great power has been sleeping
here for many long years.

554
00:56:21,070 --> 00:56:24,506
The coming of Merry and Pippin will
be like the falling of small stones...

555
00:56:24,673 --> 00:56:28,006
that starts an avalanche in the mountains.

556
00:56:28,177 --> 00:56:31,169
I n one thing you have not changed, dear friend.

557
00:56:31,346 --> 00:56:34,940
You still speak in riddles.

558
00:56:37,785 --> 00:56:44,189
A thing is about to happen that has
not happened since the Elder Days.

559
00:56:44,357 --> 00:56:47,986
The Ents are going to wake up...

560
00:56:48,528 --> 00:56:53,022
- and find that they are strong.
- Strong?!

561
00:56:53,834 --> 00:56:54,960
Oh, that's good.

562
00:56:55,168 --> 00:56:57,864
So stop your fretting, Master Dwarf.

563
00:56:58,972 --> 00:57:01,202
Merry and Pippin are quite safe.

564
00:57:01,374 --> 00:57:04,969
In fact, they are far safer than you are about to be.

565
00:57:05,145 --> 00:57:08,876
This new Gandalf's more grumpy than the old one.

566
00:57:31,170 --> 00:57:32,603
That is one of the Mearas...

567
00:57:32,772 --> 00:57:35,569
unless my eyes are cheated by some spell.

568
00:57:53,191 --> 00:57:55,455
Shadowfax.

569
00:57:58,029 --> 00:58:00,657
He is the lord of all horses...

570
00:58:02,300 --> 00:58:06,168
and has been my friend through many dangers.

571
00:58:20,417 --> 00:58:24,012
O rowan mine

572
00:58:24,188 --> 00:58:27,988
I saw you shine

573
00:58:28,158 --> 00:58:31,685
Upon a summer's day

574
00:58:32,796 --> 00:58:37,256
Upon your head How golden-red

575
00:58:37,467 --> 00:58:42,199
The crown you bore aloft

576
00:58:42,371 --> 00:58:44,771
Such a beautiful verse.

577
00:58:44,941 --> 00:58:49,844
- Is it much further?
- Bru-ra-hroom. Don't be hasty.

578
00:58:50,012 --> 00:58:53,277
You might call it far, perhaps.

579
00:58:54,183 --> 00:58:57,983
My home lies deep in the forest...

580
00:58:58,187 --> 00:59:02,089
near the roots of the mountain.

581
00:59:03,358 --> 00:59:07,021
I told Gandalf I would keep you safe.

582
00:59:07,262 --> 00:59:11,221
And safe is where I'll keep you.

583
00:59:11,499 --> 00:59:15,868
I believe you will enjoy this next one too.

584
00:59:16,271 --> 00:59:19,263
It's one of my own compositions.

585
00:59:19,441 --> 00:59:20,635
Right.

586
00:59:20,809 --> 00:59:26,941
Beneath the roof of sleeping leaves

587
00:59:27,115 --> 00:59:31,984
And the dreams of trees unfold

588
00:59:32,153 --> 00:59:38,615
When woodland halls are green and cool

589
00:59:38,827 --> 00:59:42,887
And the wind is in the West

590
00:59:43,364 --> 00:59:46,026
Come back to me

591
00:59:46,567 --> 00:59:51,026
Come back to me

592
00:59:51,204 --> 00:59:57,632
And say my land is best

593
01:00:05,084 --> 01:00:08,747
Sleep, little Shirelings.

594
01:00:08,922 --> 01:00:12,517
Heed no nightly noise.

595
01:00:12,725 --> 01:00:16,627
Sleep till morning light.

596
01:00:18,264 --> 01:00:22,428
I have business in the forest.

597
01:00:22,602 --> 01:00:28,131
There are many to call. Many that must come.

598
01:00:29,375 --> 01:00:34,039
The Shadow lies on Fangorn.

599
01:00:34,213 --> 01:00:40,048
The withering of all woods is drawing near.

600
01:00:49,493 --> 01:00:53,759
The veiling shadow that
glowers in the east takes shape.

601
01:00:54,565 --> 01:00:57,159
Sauron will suffer no rival.

602
01:00:57,601 --> 01:01:01,867
From the summit of Barad-dur,
his Eye watches ceaselessly.

603
01:01:02,039 --> 01:01:05,406
But he is not so mighty yet that he is above fear.

604
01:01:06,444 --> 01:01:08,412
Doubt ever gnaws at him.

605
01:01:08,579 --> 01:01:11,139
The rumor has reached him.

606
01:01:11,315 --> 01:01:14,284
The heir of Numenor still lives.

607
01:01:15,252 --> 01:01:18,085
Sauron fears you, Aragorn.

608
01:01:19,423 --> 01:01:21,584
He fears what you may become.

609
01:01:22,860 --> 01:01:26,295
And so he'll strike hard and fast at the world of Men.

610
01:01:26,463 --> 01:01:30,092
He will use his puppet Saruman to destroy Rohan.

611
01:01:30,266 --> 01:01:31,756
War is coming.

612
01:01:31,935 --> 01:01:35,496
Rohan must defend itself, and
therein lies our first challenge...

613
01:01:35,672 --> 01:01:38,106
for Rohan is weak and ready to fall.

614
01:01:38,274 --> 01:01:41,971
The king's mind is enslaved,
it's an old device of Saruman's.

615
01:01:42,145 --> 01:01:45,239
His hold over King Theoden is now very strong.

616
01:01:45,415 --> 01:01:50,113
Sauron and Saruman are tightening the noose.

617
01:01:50,953 --> 01:01:53,080
But for all their cunning...

618
01:01:53,288 --> 01:01:55,813
we have one advantage.

619
01:01:57,993 --> 01:02:00,553
The Ring remains hidden.

620
01:02:01,597 --> 01:02:03,497
And that we should seek to destroy it...

621
01:02:03,665 --> 01:02:06,634
has not yet entered their darkest dreams.

622
01:02:07,236 --> 01:02:10,535
And so the weapon of the enemy
is moving towards Mordor...

623
01:02:10,706 --> 01:02:12,195
in the hands of a Hobbit.

624
01:02:12,373 --> 01:02:16,469
Each day brings it closer to the fires of Mount Doom.

625
01:02:16,644 --> 01:02:19,272
We must trust now in Frodo.

626
01:02:19,447 --> 01:02:21,278
Everything depends upon speed...

627
01:02:21,449 --> 01:02:24,441
and the secrecy of his quest.

628
01:02:26,421 --> 01:02:29,754
Do not regret your decision to leave him.

629
01:02:30,625 --> 01:02:33,389
Frodo must finish this task alone.

630
01:02:34,128 --> 01:02:36,460
He's not alone.

631
01:02:36,631 --> 01:02:38,326
Sam went with him.

632
01:02:39,000 --> 01:02:40,194
Did he?

633
01:02:40,368 --> 01:02:44,998
Did he, indeed? Good.

634
01:02:45,606 --> 01:02:48,040
Yes, very good.

635
01:02:56,049 --> 01:03:00,951
The Black Gate of Mordor.

636
01:03:03,689 --> 01:03:06,157
Oh, save us.

637
01:03:11,964 --> 01:03:15,195
My old Gaffer would have a thing or
two to say if he could see us now.

638
01:03:17,436 --> 01:03:21,896
Master says to show him the way into Mordor.

639
01:03:22,074 --> 01:03:25,510
So good Smeagol does, master says so.

640
01:03:25,678 --> 01:03:26,906
I did.

641
01:03:35,688 --> 01:03:37,679
That's it, then.

642
01:03:39,258 --> 01:03:40,555
We can't get past that.

643
01:04:25,736 --> 01:04:27,067
Look!

644
01:04:27,237 --> 01:04:28,704
The gate.

645
01:04:28,872 --> 01:04:30,066
It's opening!

646
01:04:37,513 --> 01:04:39,481
I can see a way down.

647
01:04:40,216 --> 01:04:42,309
Sam, no!

648
01:04:44,520 --> 01:04:45,885
Master!

649
01:06:09,668 --> 01:06:13,195
- I do not ask you to come with me, Sam.
- I know, Mr. Frodo.

650
01:06:13,972 --> 01:06:17,135
I doubt even these Elvish cloaks will hide us in there.

651
01:06:17,576 --> 01:06:19,441
- Now!
- No!

652
01:06:20,012 --> 01:06:21,980
No! No, master!

653
01:06:22,180 --> 01:06:25,149
They catch you! They catch you!

654
01:06:26,451 --> 01:06:29,011
Don't take it to him.

655
01:06:31,957 --> 01:06:34,687
He wants the precious.

656
01:06:34,860 --> 01:06:37,886
Always he is looking for it.

657
01:06:38,063 --> 01:06:41,965
And the precious is wanting to go back to him.

658
01:06:42,200 --> 01:06:46,102
But we mustn't let him have it.

659
01:06:52,511 --> 01:06:54,604
No! There's another way.

660
01:06:54,813 --> 01:06:57,474
More secret. A dark way.

661
01:06:57,782 --> 01:07:01,445
- Why haven't you spoken of this before?
- Because master did not ask.

662
01:07:01,919 --> 01:07:02,942
He's up to something.

663
01:07:03,553 --> 01:07:06,147
Are you saying there's another way into Mordor?

664
01:07:06,323 --> 01:07:09,053
Yes. There's a path...

665
01:07:09,225 --> 01:07:11,716
and some stairs.

666
01:07:11,928 --> 01:07:13,589
And then...

667
01:07:13,763 --> 01:07:17,096
a tunnel.

668
01:07:31,114 --> 01:07:32,911
He's led us this far, Sam.

669
01:07:33,083 --> 01:07:34,482
Mr. Frodo, no.

670
01:07:35,618 --> 01:07:37,085
He's been true to his word.

671
01:07:41,958 --> 01:07:43,152
No.

672
01:07:45,294 --> 01:07:46,921
Lead the way, Smeagol.

673
01:07:47,529 --> 01:07:51,465
Good Smeagol always helps.

674
01:08:25,433 --> 01:08:26,422
Hello?

675
01:08:28,836 --> 01:08:30,895
Treebeard?

676
01:08:31,606 --> 01:08:32,936
Where has he gone?

677
01:08:33,140 --> 01:08:35,574
I had the loveliest dream last night.

678
01:08:36,209 --> 01:08:38,905
There was this large barrel, full of pipe-weed.

679
01:08:39,079 --> 01:08:41,570
And we smoked all of it. And then...

680
01:08:42,082 --> 01:08:44,016
you were sick.

681
01:08:45,619 --> 01:08:48,452
I'd give anything for a whiff of Old Toby.

682
01:08:51,958 --> 01:08:53,892
Did you hear that?

683
01:09:00,967 --> 01:09:02,366
There it is again.

684
01:09:03,303 --> 01:09:07,899
Something's not right here. Not right at all.

685
01:09:11,710 --> 01:09:14,645
You just said something... Treeish.

686
01:09:14,814 --> 01:09:18,807
No, I didn't. I was just stretching.

687
01:09:26,357 --> 01:09:28,222
You're taller.

688
01:09:28,760 --> 01:09:30,250
- Who?
- You!

689
01:09:30,428 --> 01:09:32,055
- Than what?
- Than me!

690
01:09:32,564 --> 01:09:34,691
I've always been taller than you.

691
01:09:34,866 --> 01:09:39,496
Pippin, everyone knows I'm the
tall one. You're the short one.

692
01:09:40,371 --> 01:09:41,861
Please, Merry.

693
01:09:42,073 --> 01:09:45,907
You're what? Three-foot-six? At the most?

694
01:09:46,478 --> 01:09:49,311
Whereas me, I'm pushing 3'7".

695
01:09:51,449 --> 01:09:53,713
3'8"!

696
01:09:55,653 --> 01:09:57,484
Three-foot-eight.

697
01:10:00,558 --> 01:10:02,458
You did something.

698
01:10:08,265 --> 01:10:09,857
Merry, don't! Don't drink it!

699
01:10:10,801 --> 01:10:12,267
Merry!

700
01:10:12,468 --> 01:10:14,800
No, Treebeard said that you shouldn't have any.

701
01:10:14,971 --> 01:10:18,873
- I want some!
- It could well be dangerous!

702
01:10:19,041 --> 01:10:21,202
Give me it back. Merry!

703
01:10:23,045 --> 01:10:24,410
What's happening?!

704
01:10:25,281 --> 01:10:26,748
It's got my leg!

705
01:10:27,083 --> 01:10:28,573
Merry!

706
01:10:47,970 --> 01:10:49,562
Help!

707
01:10:56,344 --> 01:10:58,209
Away with you.

708
01:10:58,380 --> 01:11:00,177
You should not be waking.

709
01:11:00,682 --> 01:11:05,551
Eat earth. Dig deep. Drink water.

710
01:11:06,154 --> 01:11:08,714
Go to sleep.

711
01:11:09,057 --> 01:11:10,922
Away with you.

712
01:11:11,092 --> 01:11:14,391
Come, the forest is waking up.

713
01:11:14,963 --> 01:11:16,896
It isn't safe.

714
01:11:19,567 --> 01:11:23,503
The trees have grown wild and dangerous.

715
01:11:23,671 --> 01:11:26,663
Anger festers in their hearts.

716
01:11:27,541 --> 01:11:29,168
Black are their thoughts.

717
01:11:29,343 --> 01:11:31,868
Strong is their hate.

718
01:11:32,046 --> 01:11:34,810
They will harm you if they can.

719
01:11:34,982 --> 01:11:38,543
There are too few of us now.

720
01:11:38,719 --> 01:11:42,711
Too few of us Ents left to manage them.

721
01:11:43,356 --> 01:11:45,984
Why are there so few of you
when you have lived so long?

722
01:11:46,159 --> 01:11:49,356
- Are there Ent children?
- Bru-ra-hroom.

723
01:11:49,529 --> 01:11:55,161
There have been no Entings for
a terrible long count of years.

724
01:11:55,368 --> 01:12:00,601
- Why is that?
- We lost the Entwives.

725
01:12:00,873 --> 01:12:02,272
Oh, I'm sorry.

726
01:12:02,375 --> 01:12:06,311
- How did they die?
- Die? No.

727
01:12:06,479 --> 01:12:09,710
We lost them.

728
01:12:09,882 --> 01:12:14,945
And now we cannot find them.

729
01:12:15,121 --> 01:12:21,355
I don't suppose you've seen Entwives in the Shire?

730
01:12:21,748 --> 01:12:24,308
Can't say that I have.

731
01:12:24,852 --> 01:12:26,877
You, Pip?

732
01:12:28,355 --> 01:12:30,754
What do they look like?

733
01:12:33,192 --> 01:12:37,856
I don't remember now.

734
01:12:54,280 --> 01:12:58,182
Edoras and the Golden Hall of Meduseld.

735
01:12:58,951 --> 01:13:01,579
There dwells Theoden, King of Rohan...

736
01:13:02,288 --> 01:13:05,155
whose mind is overthrown.

737
01:13:05,324 --> 01:13:09,590
Saruman's hold over King Theoden is now very strong.

738
01:13:10,229 --> 01:13:13,392
My lord, your son...

739
01:13:13,566 --> 01:13:15,761
he is dead.

740
01:13:17,269 --> 01:13:19,066
My lord?

741
01:13:20,338 --> 01:13:21,498
Uncle?

742
01:13:28,312 --> 01:13:30,576
Will you not go to him?

743
01:13:33,717 --> 01:13:36,117
Will you do nothing?

744
01:13:36,287 --> 01:13:38,255
Be careful what you say.

745
01:13:38,489 --> 01:13:40,616
Do not look for welcome here.

746
01:14:04,681 --> 01:14:08,811
Oh, he must have died sometime in the night.

747
01:14:09,018 --> 01:14:11,145
What a tragedy for the king...

748
01:14:11,387 --> 01:14:14,356
to lose his only son and heir.

749
01:14:15,458 --> 01:14:19,986
I understand. His passing is hard to accept.

750
01:14:20,163 --> 01:14:25,065
Especially now that your brother has deserted you.

751
01:14:25,233 --> 01:14:26,700
Leave me alone, snake!

752
01:14:28,170 --> 01:14:29,797
Oh, but you are alone.

753
01:14:31,440 --> 01:14:36,207
Who knows what you've spoken to the darkness...

754
01:14:36,378 --> 01:14:39,836
in the bitter watches of the night...

755
01:14:40,015 --> 01:14:43,678
when all your life seems to shrink.

756
01:14:43,885 --> 01:14:48,083
The walls of your bower closing in about you.

757
01:14:48,256 --> 01:14:52,817
A hutch to trammel some wild thing in.

758
01:14:55,062 --> 01:14:56,962
So fair.

759
01:14:58,232 --> 01:14:59,597
So cold.

760
01:15:01,369 --> 01:15:03,530
Like a morning of pale spring...

761
01:15:03,738 --> 01:15:07,174
still clinging to winter's chill.

762
01:15:20,955 --> 01:15:23,446
Your words are poison.

763
01:16:56,012 --> 01:16:58,480
You'll find more cheer in a graveyard.

764
01:17:12,829 --> 01:17:16,628
I cannot allow you before Theoden
King so armed, Gandalf Greyhame.

765
01:17:18,134 --> 01:17:20,694
By order of Grima Wormtongue.

766
01:17:38,052 --> 01:17:39,815
Your staff.

767
01:17:43,224 --> 01:17:46,716
You would not part an old man from his walking stick.

768
01:18:05,512 --> 01:18:08,379
My lord, Gandalf the Grey is coming.

769
01:18:16,690 --> 01:18:18,248
He's a herald of woe.

770
01:18:18,425 --> 01:18:22,862
The courtesy of your hall is
somewhat lessened of late...

771
01:18:23,964 --> 01:18:25,397
Theoden King.

772
01:18:26,099 --> 01:18:28,624
He's not welcome.

773
01:18:29,570 --> 01:18:34,906
Why should I welcome you...

774
01:18:35,409 --> 01:18:39,071
Gandalf Stormcrow?

775
01:18:39,245 --> 01:18:42,544
A just question, my liege.

776
01:18:42,715 --> 01:18:45,582
Late is the hour...

777
01:18:45,751 --> 01:18:49,709
in which this conjurer chooses to appear.

778
01:18:50,522 --> 01:18:52,581
Lathspell I name him.

779
01:18:52,757 --> 01:18:55,658
Ill news is an ill guest.

780
01:18:55,827 --> 01:19:00,389
Be silent. Keep your forked tongue behind your teeth.

781
01:19:00,565 --> 01:19:02,499
I have not passed through fire and death...

782
01:19:02,601 --> 01:19:05,832
to bandy crooked words with a witless worm.

783
01:19:06,838 --> 01:19:08,931
His staff.

784
01:19:09,140 --> 01:19:13,270
I told you to take the wizard's staff.

785
01:19:16,615 --> 01:19:18,549
Theoden...

786
01:19:19,117 --> 01:19:21,677
son of Thengel...

787
01:19:23,455 --> 01:19:25,821
too long have you sat in the Shadows.

788
01:19:28,793 --> 01:19:32,058
I would stay still if I were you.

789
01:19:32,230 --> 01:19:34,323
Hearken to me!

790
01:19:39,837 --> 01:19:41,963
I release you...

791
01:19:42,171 --> 01:19:44,139
from the spell.

792
01:19:55,685 --> 01:19:58,711
You have no power here...

793
01:19:58,888 --> 01:20:02,517
Gandalf the Grey.

794
01:20:07,930 --> 01:20:12,993
I will draw you, Saruman, as
poison is drawn from a wound.

795
01:20:22,445 --> 01:20:23,968
Wait.

796
01:20:25,414 --> 01:20:29,248
If I go, Theoden dies.

797
01:20:29,951 --> 01:20:32,146
You did not kill me...

798
01:20:32,321 --> 01:20:34,516
you will not kill him.

799
01:20:38,427 --> 01:20:40,122
Rohan is mine.

800
01:20:41,596 --> 01:20:42,927
Be gone.

801
01:21:27,440 --> 01:21:29,567
I know your face.

802
01:21:34,147 --> 01:21:35,409
Eowyn.

803
01:21:37,717 --> 01:21:38,979
Eowyn.

804
01:21:47,259 --> 01:21:48,453
Gandalf?

805
01:21:48,994 --> 01:21:51,861
Breathe the free air again, my friend.

806
01:22:05,209 --> 01:22:07,803
Dark have been my dreams of late.

807
01:22:11,949 --> 01:22:15,715
Your fingers would remember
their old strength better...

808
01:22:15,887 --> 01:22:18,856
if they grasped your sword.

809
01:23:03,966 --> 01:23:05,934
I've only...

810
01:23:06,135 --> 01:23:09,195
ever served you, my lord.

811
01:23:09,371 --> 01:23:14,365
Your leechcraft would have had me
crawling on all fours like a beast!

812
01:23:15,377 --> 01:23:17,311
Send me not from your sight.

813
01:23:19,615 --> 01:23:22,345
No, my lord! No, my lord.

814
01:23:22,551 --> 01:23:23,745
Let him go.

815
01:23:24,453 --> 01:23:27,684
Enough blood has been spilt on his account.

816
01:23:36,831 --> 01:23:39,163
Get out of my way!

817
01:23:41,402 --> 01:23:44,565
Hail, Theoden King!

818
01:24:09,162 --> 01:24:11,653
Where is Theodred?

819
01:24:14,701 --> 01:24:17,261
Where is my son?

820
01:25:44,455 --> 01:25:46,184
[Rohirric] <i> Simbelmynë. </i>
[English] Evermind.

821
01:25:51,362 --> 01:25:54,957
Ever has it grown on the tombs of my forbearers.

822
01:25:58,801 --> 01:26:01,769
Now it shall cover the grave of my son.

823
01:26:03,839 --> 01:26:07,707
Alas that these evil days should be mine.

824
01:26:08,477 --> 01:26:12,880
The young perish and the old linger.

825
01:26:13,482 --> 01:26:15,575
That I should live...

826
01:26:15,751 --> 01:26:19,118
to see the last days of my house.

827
01:26:20,389 --> 01:26:24,257
Theodred's death was not of your making.

828
01:26:27,295 --> 01:26:30,696
No parent should have to bury their child.

829
01:26:47,415 --> 01:26:49,280
He was strong in life.

830
01:26:50,384 --> 01:26:53,945
His spirit will find its way
to the halls of your fathers.

831
01:27:04,191 --> 01:27:06,491
[Rohirric] <i>Westu hál...</i>
[English] Be-thou well...

832
01:27:07,891 --> 01:27:09,891
[Rohirric] <i>Ferðu, Théodred, Ferðu.</i>
[English] Go-thou, Théodred, go-thou.

833
01:27:38,564 --> 01:27:40,464
They had no warning.

834
01:27:40,632 --> 01:27:43,032
They were unarmed.

835
01:27:43,502 --> 01:27:47,529
Now the Wild Men are moving through
the Westfold, burning as they go.

836
01:27:48,474 --> 01:27:50,442
Rick, cot and tree.

837
01:27:50,743 --> 01:27:52,973
Where is Mama?

838
01:27:53,746 --> 01:27:57,978
This is but a taste of the
terror that Saruman will unleash.

839
01:27:58,183 --> 01:28:02,517
All the more potent for he is
driven now by fear of Sauron.

840
01:28:04,123 --> 01:28:07,091
Ride out and meet him head on.

841
01:28:07,859 --> 01:28:11,351
Draw him away from your women and children.

842
01:28:11,696 --> 01:28:13,323
You must fight.

843
01:28:13,498 --> 01:28:17,332
You have 2000 good men riding north as we speak.

844
01:28:17,502 --> 01:28:19,128
Eomer is loyal to you.

845
01:28:19,302 --> 01:28:21,998
His men will return and fight for their king.

846
01:28:22,172 --> 01:28:26,074
They will be 300 leagues from here by now.

847
01:28:29,746 --> 01:28:31,976
Eomer cannot help us.

848
01:28:32,616 --> 01:28:34,379
I know what it is you want of me...

849
01:28:34,584 --> 01:28:37,849
but I will not bring further death to my people.

850
01:28:39,523 --> 01:28:41,218
I will not risk open war.

851
01:28:43,426 --> 01:28:46,793
Open war is upon you, whether you would risk it or not.

852
01:28:51,067 --> 01:28:52,694
When last I looked...

853
01:28:53,136 --> 01:28:56,765
Theoden, not Aragorn, was king of Rohan.

854
01:29:03,580 --> 01:29:05,844
Then what is the king's decision?

855
01:29:11,452 --> 01:29:12,783
By order of the king...

856
01:29:12,954 --> 01:29:14,421
the city must empty.

857
01:29:15,590 --> 01:29:18,457
We make for the refuge of Helm's Deep.

858
01:29:18,760 --> 01:29:22,662
Do not burden yourself with treasures.
Take only what provisions you need.

859
01:29:22,864 --> 01:29:24,354
Helm's Deep.

860
01:29:24,532 --> 01:29:28,059
They flee to the mountains when
they should stand and fight.

861
01:29:28,236 --> 01:29:30,204
Who will defend them if not their king?

862
01:29:30,371 --> 01:29:32,839
He's only doing what he thinks is best for his people.

863
01:29:33,007 --> 01:29:34,804
Helm's Deep has saved them in the past.

864
01:29:34,976 --> 01:29:38,878
There is no way out of that ravine.
Theoden is walking into a trap.

865
01:29:39,080 --> 01:29:41,241
He thinks he's leading them to safety.

866
01:29:41,449 --> 01:29:43,576
What they will get is a massacre.

867
01:29:45,153 --> 01:29:47,621
Theoden has a strong will, but I fear for him.

868
01:29:48,523 --> 01:29:51,856
I fear for the survival of Rohan.

869
01:29:52,327 --> 01:29:55,193
He will need you before the end, Aragorn.

870
01:29:55,662 --> 01:29:58,460
The people of Rohan will need you.

871
01:29:58,832 --> 01:30:01,300
The defenses have to hold.

872
01:30:02,736 --> 01:30:04,465
They will hold.

873
01:30:08,475 --> 01:30:10,773
The Grey Pilgrim.

874
01:30:10,944 --> 01:30:13,571
That's what they used to call me.

875
01:30:13,779 --> 01:30:18,842
Three hundred lives of Men I've walked
this earth, and now I have no time.

876
01:30:20,486 --> 01:30:22,681
With luck, my search will not be in vain.

877
01:30:23,222 --> 01:30:26,521
Look to my coming at first light on the fifth day.

878
01:30:27,393 --> 01:30:30,089
At dawn, look to the east.

879
01:30:30,263 --> 01:30:31,821
Go.

880
01:30:59,157 --> 01:31:02,490
That horse is half mad, my lord.
There's nothing you can do. Leave him.

881
01:31:03,886 --> 01:31:05,886
[Rohirric] <i>Fæste.</i>
[English] Fast.

882
01:31:06,886 --> 01:31:07,886
[Rohirric] <i>Stille nú.</i>
[English] Calm now.

883
01:31:11,186 --> 01:31:12,786
[Rohirric] <i>Fæste.</i>
[English] Fast.

884
01:31:15,086 --> 01:31:16,286
[Rohirric] <i>Stille.</i>
[English] Calm.

885
01:31:20,886 --> 01:31:22,686
[Rohirric] <i>Stille.</i>
[English] Calm.

886
01:31:24,886 --> 01:31:25,886
[Rohirric] <i>Stille.</i>
[English] Calm.

887
01:31:27,786 --> 01:31:30,185
[Rohirric] <i>Lac is drefed, gefrægon.</i>
[English] A battle is stirred up, they heard.

888
01:31:37,385 --> 01:31:38,962
[Rohirric] <i>Hwæt nemnað ðe?</i>
[English] What is your name?

889
01:31:41,531 --> 01:31:43,590
His name is Brego.

890
01:31:45,101 --> 01:31:47,001
He was my cousin's horse.

891
01:31:47,236 --> 01:31:49,033
Brego.

892
01:31:49,785 --> 01:31:51,985
[Rohirric] <i>Ðin nama is cynglic.</i>
[English] Your name is kingly.

893
01:31:54,185 --> 01:31:56,185
[Sindarin] <i>Man le trasta, Brego?</i>
[English] What troubles you, Brego?

894
01:32:01,285 --> 01:32:02,885
[Sindarin] <i>Man cenich?</i>
[English] What did you see?

895
01:32:03,753 --> 01:32:06,153
I have heard of the magic of Elves...

896
01:32:06,322 --> 01:32:09,621
but I did not look for it in a Ranger from the North.

897
01:32:10,660 --> 01:32:13,094
You speak as one of their own.

898
01:32:14,897 --> 01:32:17,330
I was raised in Rivendell...

899
01:32:17,599 --> 01:32:19,122
for a time.

900
01:32:22,436 --> 01:32:24,461
Turn this fellow free.

901
01:32:25,139 --> 01:32:27,607
He's seen enough of war.

902
01:32:39,387 --> 01:32:42,254
Gandalf the White.

903
01:32:42,423 --> 01:32:44,789
Gandalf the Fool!

904
01:32:46,060 --> 01:32:50,121
Does he seek to humble me with his newfound piety?

905
01:32:51,365 --> 01:32:55,301
There were three who followed the wizard.

906
01:32:55,703 --> 01:33:01,073
An Elf, a Dwarf and a Man.

907
01:33:01,442 --> 01:33:04,171
You stink of horse.

908
01:33:09,449 --> 01:33:11,314
The Man...

909
01:33:13,353 --> 01:33:17,551
- was he from Gondor?
- No, from the North.

910
01:33:17,724 --> 01:33:21,523
One of the Dunedain Rangers, I thought he was.

911
01:33:21,693 --> 01:33:23,490
His cloth was poor.

912
01:33:24,396 --> 01:33:29,527
And yet he bore a strange ring.

913
01:33:30,636 --> 01:33:34,163
Two serpents with emerald eyes.

914
01:33:34,373 --> 01:33:40,209
One devouring, the other crowned with golden flowers.

915
01:33:40,379 --> 01:33:42,279
The Ring of Barahir.

916
01:33:43,248 --> 01:33:46,843
So Gandalf Greyhame thinks he has found Isildur's heir.

917
01:33:47,019 --> 01:33:50,352
The lost king of Gondor. He is a fool.

918
01:33:50,522 --> 01:33:53,251
The line was broken years ago.

919
01:33:54,625 --> 01:33:56,149
It matters not.

920
01:33:56,327 --> 01:33:58,852
The world of Men shall fall.

921
01:33:59,030 --> 01:34:00,895
It will begin at Edoras.

922
01:34:10,074 --> 01:34:12,008
I am ready, Gamling.

923
01:34:12,176 --> 01:34:14,644
Bring my horse.

924
01:34:17,815 --> 01:34:19,180
This is not a defeat.

925
01:34:21,586 --> 01:34:22,814
We will return.

926
01:34:28,258 --> 01:34:30,658
We will return.

927
01:34:54,083 --> 01:34:56,017
You have some skill with a blade.

928
01:35:04,460 --> 01:35:06,553
Women of this country learned long ago:

929
01:35:06,729 --> 01:35:09,357
Those without swords can still die upon them.

930
01:35:09,532 --> 01:35:11,363
I fear neither death nor pain.

931
01:35:12,635 --> 01:35:14,728
What do you fear, my lady?

932
01:35:18,140 --> 01:35:19,971
A cage.

933
01:35:21,277 --> 01:35:25,111
To stay behind bars until use and old age accept them.

934
01:35:25,281 --> 01:35:29,181
And all chance of valor has
gone beyond recall or desire.

935
01:35:32,619 --> 01:35:34,644
You're a daughter of kings...

936
01:35:35,923 --> 01:35:39,222
a shield maiden of Rohan.

937
01:35:44,531 --> 01:35:47,022
I do not think that would be your fate.

938
01:36:20,099 --> 01:36:23,091
Theoden will not stay at Edoras.

939
01:36:23,302 --> 01:36:25,361
It's vulnerable. He knows this.

940
01:36:25,571 --> 01:36:28,472
He will expect an attack on the city.

941
01:36:29,775 --> 01:36:33,039
They will flee to Helm's Deep...

942
01:36:33,211 --> 01:36:35,543
the great fortress of Rohan.

943
01:36:36,748 --> 01:36:41,151
It is a dangerous road to take through the mountains.

944
01:36:42,587 --> 01:36:44,316
They will be slow.

945
01:36:44,689 --> 01:36:49,126
They will have women and children with them.

946
01:36:53,031 --> 01:36:55,261
Send out your Warg-riders.

947
01:37:10,114 --> 01:37:13,015
Hey, stinker, don't go getting too far ahead.

948
01:37:13,183 --> 01:37:15,845
- Why do you do that?
- What?

949
01:37:16,020 --> 01:37:18,545
Call him names. Run him down all the time.

950
01:37:18,989 --> 01:37:21,014
Because.

951
01:37:22,559 --> 01:37:24,686
Because that's what he is, Mr. Frodo.

952
01:37:24,895 --> 01:37:27,056
There's naught left in him but lies and deceit.

953
01:37:27,531 --> 01:37:30,295
It's the Ring he wants. It's all he cares about.

954
01:37:30,467 --> 01:37:32,731
You have no idea what it did to him...

955
01:37:32,903 --> 01:37:35,370
what it's still doing to him.

956
01:37:37,607 --> 01:37:39,700
I want to help him, Sam.

957
01:37:39,876 --> 01:37:41,138
Why?

958
01:37:46,449 --> 01:37:49,576
Because I have to believe he can come back.

959
01:37:53,822 --> 01:37:55,756
You can't save him, Mr. Frodo.

960
01:37:55,924 --> 01:37:58,654
What do you know about it? Nothing!

961
01:38:05,567 --> 01:38:09,765
I'm sorry, Sam. I don't know why I said that.

962
01:38:10,605 --> 01:38:11,731
I do.

963
01:38:13,775 --> 01:38:15,640
It's the Ring.

964
01:38:16,211 --> 01:38:17,769
You can't take your eyes off it.

965
01:38:18,513 --> 01:38:20,481
I've seen you.

966
01:38:20,949 --> 01:38:24,783
You're not eating. You barely sleep.

967
01:38:26,555 --> 01:38:28,785
It's taken hold of you, Mr. Frodo.

968
01:38:28,957 --> 01:38:31,653
- You have to fight it.
- I know what I have to do, Sam.

969
01:38:31,860 --> 01:38:34,795
The Ring was entrusted to me. It's my task.

970
01:38:34,963 --> 01:38:36,657
Mine! My own!

971
01:38:37,530 --> 01:38:39,623
Can't you hear yourself?

972
01:38:39,833 --> 01:38:41,494
Don't you know who you sound like?

973
01:38:51,778 --> 01:38:53,905
We wants it.

974
01:38:54,080 --> 01:38:56,776
We needs it.

975
01:38:56,950 --> 01:39:01,751
Must have the precious.

976
01:39:01,921 --> 01:39:05,288
They stole it from us.

977
01:39:05,492 --> 01:39:08,859
Sneaky little Hobbitses.

978
01:39:09,028 --> 01:39:12,930
Wicked. Tricksy. False.

979
01:39:13,099 --> 01:39:16,364
No. Not master.

980
01:39:16,536 --> 01:39:20,370
Yes, precious. False.

981
01:39:20,540 --> 01:39:25,033
They will cheat you, hurt you, lie!

982
01:39:26,178 --> 01:39:28,646
Master's my friend.

983
01:39:28,814 --> 01:39:33,877
You don't have any friends. Nobody likes you.

984
01:39:35,154 --> 01:39:37,645
Not listening. I'm not listening.

985
01:39:37,823 --> 01:39:41,815
You're a liar and a thief.

986
01:39:42,493 --> 01:39:44,017
No.

987
01:39:44,962 --> 01:39:47,863
Murderer.

988
01:39:50,334 --> 01:39:51,358
Go away.

989
01:39:51,536 --> 01:39:53,902
Go away?

990
01:39:55,907 --> 01:39:58,705
I hate you.

991
01:39:58,876 --> 01:40:01,276
I hate you.

992
01:40:01,579 --> 01:40:04,878
Where would you be without me? Gollum. Gollum.

993
01:40:05,049 --> 01:40:06,880
I saved us.

994
01:40:07,051 --> 01:40:11,578
It was me. We survived because of me.

995
01:40:12,823 --> 01:40:16,384
Not anymore.

996
01:40:17,761 --> 01:40:19,285
What did you say?

997
01:40:21,398 --> 01:40:25,232
Master looks after us now.

998
01:40:25,402 --> 01:40:28,894
We don't need you.

999
01:40:29,606 --> 01:40:31,164
What?

1000
01:40:31,341 --> 01:40:33,104
Leave now...

1001
01:40:33,276 --> 01:40:37,076
and never come back.

1002
01:40:37,247 --> 01:40:38,271
No.

1003
01:40:38,782 --> 01:40:42,980
Leave now and never come back.

1004
01:40:45,621 --> 01:40:51,526
Leave now and never come back!

1005
01:41:03,438 --> 01:41:06,134
We told him to go away.

1006
01:41:06,307 --> 01:41:09,276
And away he goes, precious.

1007
01:41:09,444 --> 01:41:11,435
Gone! Gone! Gone!

1008
01:41:11,613 --> 01:41:13,444
Smeagol is free!

1009
01:41:18,319 --> 01:41:19,809
Look.

1010
01:41:20,021 --> 01:41:24,481
Look. See what Smeagol finds?

1011
01:41:34,035 --> 01:41:35,468
They are young.

1012
01:41:35,637 --> 01:41:38,162
They are tender. They are nice.

1013
01:41:38,339 --> 01:41:41,866
Yes, they are. Eat them. Eat them!

1014
01:41:44,579 --> 01:41:46,170
You'll make him sick, you will...

1015
01:41:47,380 --> 01:41:49,575
behaving like that.

1016
01:41:52,018 --> 01:41:54,748
There's only one way to eat a brace of coneys.

1017
01:41:58,991 --> 01:42:00,515
What's it doing?

1018
01:42:01,260 --> 01:42:03,854
Stupid, fat Hobbit.

1019
01:42:04,030 --> 01:42:06,225
It ruins it.

1020
01:42:06,399 --> 01:42:10,028
What's to ruin? There's hardly any meat on them.

1021
01:42:14,173 --> 01:42:16,733
What we need is a few good taters.

1022
01:42:17,610 --> 01:42:20,670
What's taters, precious?

1023
01:42:20,846 --> 01:42:22,575
What's taters? Eh?

1024
01:42:22,748 --> 01:42:24,477
Po-ta-toes.

1025
01:42:24,817 --> 01:42:28,048
Boil them, mash them, stick them in a stew.

1026
01:42:29,589 --> 01:42:35,049
Lovely, big, golden chips with
a nice piece of fried fish.

1027
01:42:36,394 --> 01:42:38,294
Even you couldn't say no to that.

1028
01:42:38,630 --> 01:42:40,825
Oh, yes, we could.

1029
01:42:40,999 --> 01:42:44,491
Spoil a nice fish.

1030
01:42:45,770 --> 01:42:48,398
Give it to us raw...

1031
01:42:48,573 --> 01:42:51,598
and wriggling.

1032
01:42:51,775 --> 01:42:54,903
You keep nasty chips.

1033
01:42:55,846 --> 01:42:57,905
You're hopeless.

1034
01:43:10,394 --> 01:43:11,884
Mr. Frodo?

1035
01:43:29,779 --> 01:43:32,441
- Who are they?
- Wicked Men.

1036
01:43:32,649 --> 01:43:35,117
Servants of Sauron.

1037
01:43:35,918 --> 01:43:38,079
They are called to Mordor.

1038
01:43:38,287 --> 01:43:41,279
The Dark One is gathering all armies to him.

1039
01:43:41,491 --> 01:43:44,654
It won't be long now. He will soon be ready.

1040
01:43:46,229 --> 01:43:49,892
- Ready to do what?
- To make his war.

1041
01:43:50,066 --> 01:43:55,230
The last war that will cover all the world in Shadow.

1042
01:43:55,504 --> 01:43:58,564
We've got to get moving. Come on, Sam.

1043
01:43:58,740 --> 01:43:59,968
Mr. Frodo.

1044
01:44:00,475 --> 01:44:02,102
Look.

1045
01:44:05,681 --> 01:44:07,979
It's an oliphaunt.

1046
01:44:16,190 --> 01:44:19,216
No one at home will believe this.

1047
01:44:30,371 --> 01:44:32,236
Smeagol?

1048
01:45:12,611 --> 01:45:15,079
We've lingered here too long.

1049
01:45:18,083 --> 01:45:19,414
Come on, Sam.

1050
01:45:32,898 --> 01:45:35,594
Wait! We're innocent travelers!

1051
01:45:37,302 --> 01:45:42,399
There are no travelers in this land.
Only servants of the Dark Tower.

1052
01:45:42,574 --> 01:45:45,474
We are bound to an errand of secrecy.

1053
01:45:46,878 --> 01:45:50,245
Those that claim to oppose the
enemy would do well not to hinder us.

1054
01:45:50,414 --> 01:45:52,439
The enemy?

1055
01:45:54,552 --> 01:45:58,044
His sense of duty was no less than yours, I deem.

1056
01:46:00,490 --> 01:46:02,549
You wonder what his name is...

1057
01:46:04,060 --> 01:46:06,324
where he came from.

1058
01:46:08,298 --> 01:46:10,732
And if he was really evil at heart.

1059
01:46:12,402 --> 01:46:15,860
What lies or threats led him
on this long march from home.

1060
01:46:17,474 --> 01:46:19,965
If he would not rather have stayed there...

1061
01:46:22,179 --> 01:46:23,669
in peace.

1062
01:46:27,250 --> 01:46:30,276
War will make corpses of us all.

1063
01:46:30,453 --> 01:46:32,511
Bind their hands.

